1
00:00:52,702 --> 00:00:54,097
Hey, take it easy.

2
00:00:54,097 --> 00:00:57,111
Let me let loose a little.

3
00:01:01,951 --> 00:01:03,614
You've been back from London for almost a month.

4
00:01:03,614 --> 00:01:05,939
Aren't you going home?

5
00:01:05,939 --> 00:01:10,879
I just finished my degree in Strategic Management, it wasn't easy.

6
00:01:10,879 --> 00:01:12,873
I just want to take a break

7
00:01:12,873 --> 00:01:15,447
But you've been partying every day!

8
00:01:15,447 --> 00:01:17,658
Does your dad know?

9
00:01:17,658 --> 00:01:20,709
Not and'—if Dad doesn't know, it's not a mistake.

10
00:01:21,823 --> 00:01:22,569
Cheers!

11
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:02,123
Hello!

12
00:02:02,123 --> 00:02:04,275
"Ya, it's Dad."

13
00:02:06,193 --> 00:02:06,776
Hello...

14
00:02:06,776 --> 00:02:12,749
Hello!! Dad.. @#$% Dad, the signal is bad.

15
00:02:15,191 --> 00:02:16,629
"Are you in Bangkok already?"

16
00:02:18,608 --> 00:02:20,738
(Shit! who told dad that)

17
00:02:23,190 --> 00:02:24,887
I just landed.

18
00:02:24,887 --> 00:02:27,249
I was going to surprise you.

19
00:02:27,249 --> 00:02:30,239
"Well, hurry and come surprise me."

20
00:02:30,239 --> 00:02:32,783
"I have something to talk with you."

21
00:02:32,783 --> 00:02:33,972
okay.

22
00:02:33,972 --> 00:02:35,456
I'll be there to meet you soon.

23
00:02:37,314 --> 00:02:40,360
My God!...
Does Dad know everything?

24
00:03:33,056 --> 00:03:35,307
"Auntie?"

25
00:03:35,307 --> 00:03:36,941
"Auntie, are you there?"

26
00:03:36,941 --> 00:03:40,305
"Yeah, I heard you.."

27
00:03:40,305 --> 00:03:41,964
Oh, Din.

28
00:03:41,964 --> 00:03:43,911
Aren't you going to work?

29
00:03:43,911 --> 00:03:46,479
I'm off today, so I'm not working.

30
00:03:48,429 --> 00:03:50,324
Oh, I forgot.

31
00:03:50,324 --> 00:03:52,549
What's up?

32
00:03:52,549 --> 00:03:54,317
I saw you complaining about knee pain,

33
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:56,659
so I made this cane for you.

34
00:03:56,659 --> 00:03:59,005
Try it out to see if it fits.

35
00:04:00,428 --> 00:04:01,157
็Hey!!!

36
00:04:01,157 --> 00:04:02,692
That's awesome.

37
00:04:02,692 --> 00:04:05,022
Thank you, Din.

38
00:04:07,677 --> 00:04:09,274
So, will it be strong?

39
00:04:09,274 --> 00:04:10,135
Oh, Auntie!

40
00:04:10,135 --> 00:04:14,889
I used high-quality pipe, grade 13.5. It's guaranteed to be strong and durable.

41
00:04:14,889 --> 00:04:17,509
You see, I made a double-layered base for it, too.

42
00:04:17,592 --> 00:04:20,715
It will help distribute the weight better.

43
00:04:23,008 --> 00:04:23,532
Do you see?

44
00:04:23,532 --> 00:04:26,008
Hey, that's good.

45
00:04:26,008 --> 00:04:27,725
Good support.

46
00:04:27,725 --> 00:04:29,371
Thanks!!

47
00:04:38,506 --> 00:04:39,132
Yeah, Auntie.

48
00:04:39,132 --> 00:04:39,632
Hmm?

49
00:04:39,632 --> 00:04:41,085
Are you using the water?

50
00:04:42,172 --> 00:04:42,672
No!

51
00:04:43,756 --> 00:04:46,089
I hear a hissing sound, like a water leak.

52
00:04:49,047 --> 00:04:50,898
Has the water bill for your room gone up lately?

53
00:04:50,898 --> 00:04:54,165
It is getting more expensive, though.

54
00:04:54,165 --> 00:04:58,025
But I think they've raised the price.

55
00:04:59,379 --> 00:05:00,449
Let me go in and take a look.

56
00:05:00,449 --> 00:05:02,342
I think we have a leak.

57
00:05:02,342 --> 00:05:04,641
That explains the high water bill.

58
00:05:14,085 --> 00:05:14,668
Any luck?

59
00:05:14,668 --> 00:05:16,394
Found it.

60
00:05:18,001 --> 00:05:19,796
So it is a leak?

61
00:05:31,583 --> 00:05:32,218
Auntie Tai.

62
00:05:32,218 --> 00:05:32,718
Yes!

63
00:05:35,166 --> 00:05:35,968
Definitely.

64
00:05:35,968 --> 00:05:37,946
There's definitely a leak in this pipe.

65
00:05:38,957 --> 00:05:39,478
Really?

66
00:05:39,478 --> 00:05:40,638
Yes, really.

67
00:05:42,123 --> 00:05:43,601
But I can fix it for you.

68
00:05:43,601 --> 00:05:45,208
I happen to have a spare pipe.

69
00:05:45,208 --> 00:05:46,793
But let me go get some cement first.

70
00:05:46,793 --> 00:05:48,857
Thank you so much, Din

71
00:05:50,164 --> 00:05:51,170
How did it leak?

72
00:05:51,170 --> 00:05:52,044
That's a good question, Auntie.

73
00:07:11,986 --> 00:07:12,849
Oh!!!

74
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:14,234
Shit!!

75
00:07:14,234 --> 00:07:18,366
@#@$$# Ugh, why did it have to go flat today?

76
00:07:18,366 --> 00:07:19,471
And I'm already in a rush.

77
00:07:19,471 --> 00:07:25,235
Aaaah!

78
00:07:25,610 --> 00:07:26,381
[Cries out in pain] Ouch!

79
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:28,151
[Din calls out surprised] Heyyy!

80
00:07:29,859 --> 00:07:30,699
What the hell is this?

81
00:07:30,699 --> 00:07:33,257
Oh... I'm so sorry!

82
00:07:33,257 --> 00:07:37,150
I'm so sorry!

83
00:07:37,150 --> 00:07:38,744
I'm so sorry!!

84
00:07:41,483 --> 00:07:43,576
Hey! Hey!

85
00:07:58,564 --> 00:07:59,419
I'm sorry.

86
00:07:59,419 --> 00:08:01,911
Um... I was just going to ask...

87
00:08:01,911 --> 00:08:04,425
Do you know how to change a tire?

88
00:08:04,425 --> 00:08:06,243
Yeah, I do.

89
00:08:08,521 --> 00:08:09,224
Lift it up.

90
00:08:09,224 --> 00:08:10,816
Huh?

91
00:08:10,816 --> 00:08:13,161
Wait, wait, wait... hold on!

92
00:08:15,812 --> 00:08:16,609
you!

93
00:08:16,609 --> 00:08:18,047
Hey! We just met!

94
00:08:18,047 --> 00:08:19,909
How can you ask me to lift my skirt?!

95
00:08:19,909 --> 00:08:22,379
Ya: Woah, we literally just met for the first time!
Din: Wait, wait, wait

96
00:08:22,379 --> 00:08:23,960
What the hell?

97
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:25,328
Ya: Are you out of your mind?!
Din: I meant open the hood of the car!

98
00:08:25,328 --> 00:08:27,635
I need to get a wrench to fix your car!

99
00:08:29,601 --> 00:08:32,518
Oh! I totally misunderstood. I'm so sorry!

100
00:08:32,518 --> 00:08:34,036
Well, you weren't being clear!

101
00:08:34,036 --> 00:08:36,425
Sorry about that...

102
00:08:39,392 --> 00:08:40,455
Are you okay? Did that hurt?

103
00:08:40,455 --> 00:08:42,320
Sorry about that...

104
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:43,707
I'm sorry!!

105
00:08:43,707 --> 00:08:45,312
Right this way, please.

106
00:08:50,224 --> 00:08:53,390
I'll leave it to you then. Sorry about that, and thank you so much!

107
00:09:03,222 --> 00:09:03,741
Here you go.

108
00:09:05,514 --> 00:09:06,819
Is there anything I can do to help?

109
00:09:10,721 --> 00:09:11,302
Is it this one?

110
00:09:20,303 --> 00:09:21,289
Hold on.

111
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:24,038
If you want me to change your tire,

112
00:09:24,038 --> 00:09:25,513
go stand over there.

113
00:09:26,427 --> 00:09:27,029
You're in the way.

114
00:09:28,844 --> 00:09:30,813
Oh! Take your time then.

115
00:09:30,813 --> 00:09:36,083
Sure thing! Take your time, and just let me know if you need anything!

116
00:10:19,796 --> 00:10:21,049
Mind if I join you?

117
00:10:23,254 --> 00:10:24,504
All the other tables are full.

118
00:10:26,628 --> 00:10:27,521
Hey beautiful,

119
00:10:27,521 --> 00:10:28,802
can I order, please?

120
00:10:32,502 --> 00:10:33,284
Thank you.

121
00:10:33,284 --> 00:10:36,285
Kanghan : I'll have a duck noodle soup, please.
Server : Sure thing!

122
00:10:36,285 --> 00:10:38,124
Make it a large, please

123
00:10:53,541 --> 00:10:55,658
Hey... do you really eat noodles with a spoon and fork?

124
00:10:58,207 --> 00:10:58,934
Looks pretty bougie.

125
00:10:58,934 --> 00:11:00,017
Huh?

126
00:11:00,017 --> 00:11:02,957
Huh? What?

127
00:11:03,790 --> 00:11:04,487
Bougie?

128
00:11:04,487 --> 00:11:08,748
Who said that? Nah, it's nothing.

129
00:11:08,748 --> 00:11:12,273
I'm just kidding! Nothing at all, go ahead and eat.

130
00:11:13,539 --> 00:11:14,066
My bad.

131
00:11:16,955 --> 00:11:18,032
Thank you!

132
00:11:24,121 --> 00:11:25,735
"Ah... it’s freaking hot outside!

133
00:11:46,409 --> 00:11:51,367
(Slurp!)

134
00:12:03,366 --> 00:12:04,032
(Clink!) (Vinegar splashes)

135
00:12:09,323 --> 00:12:10,041
A bit too sweet!

136
00:12:20,988 --> 00:12:22,405
(Clink!) (Vinegar splashes)

137
00:12:27,612 --> 00:12:28,541
Mmm-hmm...

138
00:12:28,541 --> 00:12:29,878
A bit too sour, too."

139
00:12:35,028 --> 00:12:36,376
(Laughs) Okay, I'll stop messing with you.

140
00:12:46,027 --> 00:12:46,918
Awesome!

141
00:12:55,359 --> 00:13:02,057
(Loud soda slurping)

142
00:13:03,858 --> 00:13:05,131
(Burping)

143
00:13:14,773 --> 00:13:15,766
Thank you very much.

144
00:13:19,939 --> 00:13:20,439
Hey!

145
00:13:30,563 --> 00:13:31,143
What the heck?

146
00:13:32,479 --> 00:13:33,395
He didn't even finish...

147
00:13:47,894 --> 00:13:50,850
Mr. Theerach Woranantakul

148
00:13:52,018 --> 00:13:52,528
(Tsk)

149
00:13:53,851 --> 00:13:54,430
Great.

150
00:13:54,430 --> 00:13:56,267
Well, I'm screwed.

151
00:13:56,267 --> 00:13:57,501
Where am I supposed to find him?

152
00:14:01,059 --> 00:14:01,894
(Sighs)

153
00:14:05,142 --> 00:14:05,953
Guess I'll take this, then.

154
00:14:24,014 --> 00:14:25,214
Here's some water.

155
00:14:27,597 --> 00:14:28,609
Thank you so much.

156
00:14:28,609 --> 00:14:30,855
Thank you so much, really.

157
00:14:34,429 --> 00:14:36,034
And... I'm so sorry about earlier.

158
00:14:36,034 --> 00:14:38,837
I'm so sorry, and thank you so much.

159
00:14:38,837 --> 00:14:41,757
And don't go kicking anyone else in the crotch, alright?

160
00:15:05,092 --> 00:15:07,411
Is champagne all you care about now?

161
00:15:07,411 --> 00:15:10,088
Moët is over ten thousand a bottle.

162
00:15:12,050 --> 00:15:14,337
I just wanted to give it a try, Dad.

163
00:15:14,337 --> 00:15:15,932
Just a try, huh?

164
00:15:15,932 --> 00:15:18,721
20 bottles is over 200,000 baht!

165
00:15:18,721 --> 00:15:20,829
I'm so sorry, Dad.

166
00:15:20,829 --> 00:15:23,310
I didn't think it would be that much.

167
00:15:25,798 --> 00:15:27,467
What are you planning to do now that you've graduated?

168
00:15:27,467 --> 00:15:30,781
Well... once everything is settled,

169
00:15:30,781 --> 00:15:32,347
I'll go apply for a job.

170
00:15:32,347 --> 00:15:33,816
Apply for a job?

171
00:15:33,816 --> 00:15:36,889
Why don't you work at my company?

172
00:15:36,889 --> 00:15:39,897
I don't really want to, Dad.

173
00:15:39,897 --> 00:15:40,824
Why not?

174
00:15:42,504 --> 00:15:44,818
Well... I just don't want to sell pipes, Dad

175
00:15:47,795 --> 00:15:49,285
What's wrong with selling pipes?

176
00:15:49,285 --> 00:15:53,004
Dad, I graduated with a degree in Strategic Management...

177
00:15:53,004 --> 00:15:58,961
and it was really tough. I just want to do something smart and with a good future.

178
00:16:00,002 --> 00:16:02,837
Smart? A good future?

179
00:16:02,837 --> 00:16:05,074
All day in meetings,

180
00:16:05,074 --> 00:16:07,093
speaking Thai and English,

181
00:16:07,093 --> 00:16:09,836
and coming home to drink $300 champagne?!

182
00:16:11,209 --> 00:16:14,000
That's... that's not what I meant, Dad.

183
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:18,271
I just want to do something I'm proud of, and make you proud too, Dad.

184
00:16:18,271 --> 00:16:20,832
I'm proud of what I do.

185
00:16:20,832 --> 00:16:24,062
Because these pipes... aren't just pipes.

186
00:16:24,062 --> 00:16:27,406
They carry the water that sustains people's lives...

187
00:16:27,406 --> 00:16:32,071
Our work is a life system. It's not glamorous, it's not cool...

188
00:16:32,071 --> 00:16:34,459
but it keeps people alive.

189
00:16:34,459 --> 00:16:40,621
I understand, Dad... but I studied Strategic Management. I really don't want to do this

190
00:16:40,621 --> 00:16:43,359
"I don't want to deal with technicians, and I hate being a salesperson...

191
00:16:43,359 --> 00:16:45,973
I just don't want to get rejected, Dad.

192
00:16:45,973 --> 00:16:50,674
But today, you're living off the money of the very people you look down on.

193
00:16:50,674 --> 00:16:53,631
"I didn't mean it like that, Dad.

194
00:16:54,870 --> 00:16:55,784
Let's just say...

195
00:16:55,784 --> 00:16:57,941
I didn't bring you here to sell pipes.

196
00:16:57,941 --> 00:16:59,681
Then what do you want me to do, Dad?

197
00:16:59,681 --> 00:17:03,515
Tomorrow, go to my company...

198
00:17:03,515 --> 00:17:07,582
see Khun Amata. Dress simple,

199
00:17:07,582 --> 00:17:14,736
go in, and start working...

200
00:17:14,736 --> 00:17:15,236
without letting anyone know you're my daughter.

201
00:17:15,236 --> 00:17:19,242
You're going to intern as a Management Trainee

202
00:17:19,242 --> 00:17:20,579
What??

203
00:17:20,579 --> 00:17:22,230
Do I look like I'm joking?

204
00:17:22,230 --> 00:17:24,949
First week, you go to the warehouse...

205
00:17:24,949 --> 00:17:28,508
count the stock, see how tough this business really is.

206
00:17:28,508 --> 00:17:34,126
Second week, you shadow the technicians. Third week, I'm hosting 'The Next Leader'...

207
00:17:34,126 --> 00:17:38,715
You need to find candidates to compete... and most importantly, you have to win.

208
00:17:38,715 --> 00:17:41,476
(Sighs)... And what if I don't?

209
00:17:41,476 --> 00:17:44,541
Fine... so you won't do it?

210
00:17:44,541 --> 00:17:46,424
Deal!

211
00:17:47,613 --> 00:17:48,113
Fine....

212
00:17:50,654 --> 00:17:52,725
Then I'll just freeze all your credit cards.

213
00:17:54,195 --> 00:17:59,278
The car you drive is in my name. If you want to use it, pay up.

214
00:17:59,278 --> 00:18:03,307
(Fake sobs) Oh... my... god..."

215
00:18:03,307 --> 00:18:11,110
Daddy!! Don't you love me anymore?!

216
00:18:11,110 --> 00:18:16,551
Who does that... sending their own daughter to suffer out of nowhere?! (Fake sobs)

217
00:18:17,526 --> 00:18:18,203
Hold on.

218
00:18:18,203 --> 00:18:19,684
Look up there.

219
00:18:25,358 --> 00:18:27,009
Don't cry in here.

220
00:18:27,009 --> 00:18:29,128
I'm not a kid anymore, Dad!

221
00:18:29,128 --> 00:18:31,216
I'm teaching you like an adult.

222
00:18:31,216 --> 00:18:35,205
Adults take responsibility for their spending.

223
00:18:35,205 --> 00:18:39,912
If you manage well, lead people well, and win 'The Next Leader',

224
00:18:39,912 --> 00:18:42,009
I'll give everything back to you.

225
00:18:53,021 --> 00:18:57,746
Ugh, Dad... Where on earth am I going to find someone to compete for me?!

226
00:19:00,312 --> 00:19:03,203
Alright! Operation: Prove Myself starts now!

227
00:19:19,518 --> 00:19:23,438
Ow! Why does it have to be bad luck from the very first step?!

228
00:19:34,766 --> 00:19:35,500
Thank you.

229
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:37,698
Wait... You?!

230
00:19:37,698 --> 00:19:38,703
Hey!!

231
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:46,017
Oh! We've actually met before!

232
00:19:46,017 --> 00:19:47,741
Aren't you going to say hi?

233
00:19:47,741 --> 00:19:51,733
"Woah!! What the... How rude!

234
00:19:51,733 --> 00:19:53,610
"Ugh...!!!"

235
00:20:34,175 --> 00:20:34,843
Hey, Bro.

236
00:20:38,424 --> 00:20:38,924
Who's your 'Bro'?

237
00:20:39,882 --> 00:20:42,757
You, obviously. You're older, so you're the older one.

238
00:20:44,048 --> 00:20:45,563
How do you even know I'm older?

239
00:20:47,423 --> 00:20:49,642
I just know. Maybe I have a sixth sense.

240
00:20:49,642 --> 00:20:53,360
I can read fortunes, too.

241
00:20:54,505 --> 00:20:55,302
Want a reading, Bro?

242
00:20:55,302 --> 00:20:57,212
No.!!

243
00:20:57,212 --> 00:20:59,268
Pointless. A waste of time.

244
00:20:59,268 --> 00:21:01,026
I'm out.

245
00:21:01,026 --> 00:21:03,617
Hey!! Just try it first... Sit down!

246
00:21:03,617 --> 00:21:06,422
Sit down!

247
00:21:06,422 --> 00:21:07,948
Hey! ...

248
00:21:07,948 --> 00:21:15,841
Hmm, believe me or not, today you'll definitely find what you've been looking for.

249
00:21:18,669 --> 00:21:19,446
What's that supposed to mean?

250
00:21:19,446 --> 00:21:22,370
What does it mean, huh...?

251
00:21:22,370 --> 00:21:26,343
Ta-da-da-daaa...!

252
00:21:26,343 --> 00:21:29,357
Hey!! Where did you find that?!

253
00:21:33,292 --> 00:21:35,139
You left it at the noodle shop yesterday, Bro...

254
00:21:35,139 --> 00:21:38,168
I knew it... You looked so familiar.

255
00:21:38,168 --> 00:21:40,084
Turns out we work at the same company.

256
00:21:40,084 --> 00:21:41,233
Just give it back already.

257
00:21:42,999 --> 00:21:43,786
Let me take a look...

258
00:21:43,786 --> 00:21:44,924
Whoa!!

259
00:21:44,924 --> 00:21:46,924
Gimme that.

260
00:21:57,664 --> 00:21:58,922
Okay, okay... I'll stop.

261
00:22:01,788 --> 00:22:02,708
Enjoy your meal!

262
00:22:41,325 --> 00:22:41,825
Din,

263
00:22:41,825 --> 00:22:42,859
come over here for a sec...

264
00:22:49,657 --> 00:22:51,689
Measure this first, and I'll be back to check... Coming,

265
00:22:51,689 --> 00:22:52,438
Okay.

266
00:22:52,438 --> 00:22:53,956
Kub, P'Chong.

267
00:22:53,956 --> 00:22:57,461
Din... this is Ya, the MT intern.

268
00:22:58,698 --> 00:22:59,508
Suki vendor?

269
00:22:59,508 --> 00:23:00,923
That's MK.

270
00:23:00,923 --> 00:23:02,385
Got roasted duck, then?!

271
00:23:02,385 --> 00:23:03,616
Hey, you!

272
00:23:03,616 --> 00:23:06,145
Hey, okay, that's enough...

273
00:23:06,145 --> 00:23:07,917
Din, stop messing with her.

274
00:23:07,917 --> 00:23:08,538
Okay.

275
00:23:08,538 --> 00:23:10,154
Initiating her on day one, huh?

276
00:23:10,154 --> 00:23:14,278
Go on... take her to check the stock. Take good care of her.

277
00:23:14,278 --> 00:23:17,082
Brief her on the PVC pipes.

278
00:23:17,082 --> 00:23:19,040
But I'm training Kanghan right now.

279
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:21,464
Kanghan!!

280
00:23:21,464 --> 00:23:21,964
Yes, sir!

281
00:23:21,964 --> 00:23:22,892
You good with that?

282
00:23:22,892 --> 00:23:24,652
Sure thing!

283
00:23:24,652 --> 00:23:26,112
Yeah, sorted then.

284
00:23:26,112 --> 00:23:29,585
Alright. And Din... don't mess with her too much,

285
00:23:29,585 --> 00:23:30,606
got it?

286
00:23:30,606 --> 00:23:31,509
Take good care of her.

287
00:23:36,818 --> 00:23:37,581
Right this way

288
00:23:53,607 --> 00:23:56,825
There are actually many types of PVC pipes, categorized by their use.

289
00:23:56,825 --> 00:23:59,711
Blue PVC pipes are for drinking water, based on TIS standards."

290
00:23:59,711 --> 00:24:02,321
Yellow pipes are for electrical conduits, based on TIS standards.

291
00:24:02,321 --> 00:24:04,616
But nowadays, they also come in white and black.

292
00:24:04,616 --> 00:24:07,227
Grey pipes are for agricultural use.

293
00:24:07,227 --> 00:24:10,145
White pipes are for sanitary systems, ideal for exposed piping.

294
00:24:10,145 --> 00:24:13,057
But this section right here is all about plumbing.

295
00:24:13,057 --> 00:24:15,853
They're categorized into 5 pressure classes.

296
00:24:15,853 --> 00:24:21,134
Including Class 5, 7, 8.5, 10.5, and 13.5.

297
00:24:21,134 --> 00:24:24,338
The higher the number, the thicker it is, and the more pressure it can take.

298
00:24:24,338 --> 00:24:27,149
And they're also split by pipe ends, see?

299
00:24:27,149 --> 00:24:36,427
Pipe ends come in plain and bell-end. Bell-ends have two types: solvent cement joint, and rubber ring joint, also known as push-fit pipes.

300
00:24:36,427 --> 00:24:40,306
Mmm... How do you know so much? Impressive!

301
00:24:40,306 --> 00:24:44,209
My dad's a handyman. I've heard this since I was a kid. You should know this too, you know.

302
00:24:44,209 --> 00:24:49,799
Awesome! Knowledgeable AND handy! Hey, did you see the sign in front of the company?

303
00:24:49,799 --> 00:24:52,346
Yeah, I saw it... It's just the company sign.

304
00:24:52,346 --> 00:24:56,711
No, not that... I mean 'The Next Leader' project sign. Interested in joining?

305
00:24:56,711 --> 00:24:58,229
"Nah!

306
00:24:59,641 --> 00:25:06,486
Hey... wait a sec! This is done by department, so the winner has a real shot at becoming a lead!

307
00:25:06,486 --> 00:25:10,530
You get a raise, plus a 300,000 baht cash prize!

308
00:25:10,530 --> 00:25:11,656
Okay?

309
00:25:11,656 --> 00:25:13,332
Nah, waste of time.

310
00:25:13,332 --> 00:25:17,297
Come on, give it a shot! Your talent would go to waste!

311
00:25:17,297 --> 00:25:19,907
If you enter, you'll definitely win!

312
00:25:19,907 --> 00:25:22,797
Hold on... whether I compete or not, what's it to you?

313
00:25:22,797 --> 00:25:25,803
I just mean well! I can see you're super talented.

314
00:25:25,803 --> 00:25:27,056
Nope.

315
00:25:27,056 --> 00:25:29,649
Come on... just give it a try!

316
00:25:30,553 --> 00:25:35,760
Look at you! Talented, smart, and handsome!

317
00:25:35,760 --> 00:25:41,442
Great handy skills, highly knowledgeable, and your personality is... decent.

318
00:25:42,885 --> 00:25:45,699
Flattering me like this... do you have a thing for me?

319
00:25:46,593 --> 00:25:47,535
And what if I do?

320
00:25:50,009 --> 00:25:52,536
Just kidding... I just mean well, you know!

321
00:25:54,050 --> 00:25:55,354
Thanks for the good intentions...

322
00:25:55,354 --> 00:25:56,862
But I'm still not competing.

323
00:25:56,862 --> 00:25:59,004
End of story, Miss MK.

324
00:26:00,341 --> 00:26:01,046
It's MT, jeez!

325
00:26:27,713 --> 00:26:29,999
Hey!! Bro, didn't you see the glue on the floor?!

326
00:26:31,129 --> 00:26:31,837
Woah, woah, woah!!

327
00:26:34,587 --> 00:26:37,096
Wait, so you work in this department?

328
00:26:37,096 --> 00:26:40,126
This is my domain right here!

329
00:26:40,126 --> 00:26:42,747
So, are you working at the shop today?

330
00:26:42,747 --> 00:26:44,249
Mmm-hmm..

331
00:26:44,249 --> 00:26:45,916
Sweet! Come on over then.

332
00:26:45,916 --> 00:26:47,493
Give me a hand here, quick!

333
00:26:47,493 --> 00:26:49,618
Yeah, hurry up! Come on!"

334
00:26:51,293 --> 00:26:51,832
Help with what?

335
00:26:51,832 --> 00:26:53,618
First things first... put on these gloves."

336
00:26:56,917 --> 00:26:57,988
Gloves?...

337
00:26:57,988 --> 00:27:00,923
Why are they so filthy?!

338
00:27:08,291 --> 00:27:09,993
Here, hold this for me.

339
00:27:09,993 --> 00:27:12,783
Hold?

340
00:27:12,783 --> 00:27:14,783
Which part?

341
00:27:14,783 --> 00:27:15,283
Anywhere, just don't let it tilt.

342
00:27:15,283 --> 00:27:16,608
Hurry!

343
00:27:16,608 --> 00:27:18,831
Move it over a bit more...

344
00:27:18,831 --> 00:27:21,178
Don't let it tilt, huh?...

345
00:27:21,178 --> 00:27:22,355
Hold on a sec...

346
00:27:30,913 --> 00:27:33,519
You're quite a perfectionist, huh? You really love having everything organized.

347
00:27:33,519 --> 00:27:35,471
Isn't that just how it should be?

348
00:27:40,078 --> 00:27:41,039
True that.

349
00:27:46,036 --> 00:27:46,805
Hold it right there.

350
00:27:46,805 --> 00:27:47,305
Hmmm.

351
00:27:51,743 --> 00:27:55,368
So, what's your major?... Engineering?

352
00:27:55,368 --> 00:27:56,842
Mmhmm.

353
00:27:56,842 --> 00:27:59,146
Mechanical engineering.

354
00:27:59,146 --> 00:28:01,512
Ah... Was it hard?

355
00:28:01,512 --> 00:28:02,920
Not really.

356
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:05,366
Perfect!

357
00:28:05,366 --> 00:28:11,342
So, what's next, I wonder?...

358
00:28:11,342 --> 00:28:14,133
How much was it again?...

359
00:28:20,115 --> 00:28:20,809
"Woah!!"

360
00:28:20,809 --> 00:28:24,023
Hey, let me see!

361
00:28:24,023 --> 00:28:24,905
Are you alright?

362
00:28:24,905 --> 00:28:27,939
Take it off and let me see. Are you okay?

363
00:28:27,939 --> 00:28:30,391
Is it bleeding?..

364
00:28:30,391 --> 00:28:33,076
It's nothing... I'm fine.

365
00:28:33,076 --> 00:28:34,152
Just a scratch.

366
00:28:34,152 --> 00:28:36,057
Let me see again! It's turning red.

367
00:28:36,057 --> 00:28:37,691
I'm fine, it's really nothing.

368
00:28:39,904 --> 00:28:41,703
I better go to the restroom first.

369
00:28:41,703 --> 00:28:43,377
I'll be right back.

370
00:28:44,612 --> 00:28:45,270
Are you sure about that?.

371
00:29:28,898 --> 00:29:32,762
Hello, Dad? It looks like it’s going to rain. Can you send P'Chok to pick me up?

372
00:29:32,762 --> 00:29:36,403
Please?.. Otherwise I don't know how I'll get home.

373
00:29:38,230 --> 00:29:40,071
Okay.. Thank you, Dad!

374
00:30:22,641 --> 00:30:23,846
Oh.. it's you..

375
00:30:24,974 --> 00:30:25,766
Didn't you bring an umbrella?

376
00:30:25,766 --> 00:30:29,455
It's fine, really... You keep it.

377
00:30:29,455 --> 00:30:31,471
It's fine, I'm lending it to you.

378
00:30:31,471 --> 00:30:34,055
Just take it for now.

379
00:30:35,806 --> 00:30:37,125
Wait, you don't have to...

380
00:30:37,125 --> 00:30:38,416
Someone's coming to pick me up soon.

381
00:30:55,553 --> 00:30:56,308
Auntie Tai!!

382
00:30:57,261 --> 00:30:58,636
Hey! Din!

383
00:30:58,678 --> 00:30:59,671
Where have you been? You're carrying so much.

384
00:30:59,671 --> 00:31:00,756
AUNTIE!!!"

385
00:31:00,756 --> 00:31:01,992
[Car horn blaring]

386
00:31:01,992 --> 00:31:02,497
Screaming]

387
00:31:14,134 --> 00:31:14,754
Auntie Tai...

388
00:31:14,754 --> 00:31:17,003
Auntie...

389
00:31:17,003 --> 00:31:24,052
Auntie Tai...

390
00:31:24,052 --> 00:31:26,014
Auntie Tai!! Wake up!!

391
00:31:26,014 --> 00:31:29,111
Talk to me, Auntie Tai!!

392
00:31:29,111 --> 00:31:38,939
Auntie Tai....!!

393
00:31:51,504 --> 00:31:53,617
The patient's leg is quite severely injured...

394
00:31:53,617 --> 00:31:55,379
Do you really have no friends left?

395
00:31:55,379 --> 00:31:59,878
Actually, I just want to sit with you, Bro.

396
00:31:59,878 --> 00:32:00,886
But I don't want to!

397
00:32:00,886 --> 00:32:03,056
Do you really not want to compete in The Next Leader?

398
00:32:03,056 --> 00:32:06,124
If I win, I get the prize money, right?

399
00:32:06,124 --> 00:32:08,991
Absolutely. 300,000 baht.

400
00:32:10,168 --> 00:32:10,668
Deal?

401
00:32:13,668 --> 00:32:14,300
Watch out!

402
00:32:14,300 --> 00:32:16,467
I'm Phong.

403
00:32:16,467 --> 00:32:18,593
I just moved here to manage this project.

404
00:32:18,593 --> 00:32:23,220
I heard Ms. Ya is assembly a team for The Next Leader?

405
00:32:23,220 --> 00:32:25,087
Can I volunteer to help out?

406
00:32:25,087 --> 00:32:27,626
Looking like that, he's totally jealous.

407
00:32:27,626 --> 00:32:29,694
"Is this what you meant by 'not lying'?

408
00:32:29,694 --> 00:32:31,188
What did I lie to you about?

409
00:32:31,188 --> 00:32:32,470
For your own personal gain.

410
00:32:32,470 --> 00:32:35,529
Actually, you don't need to care so much about Din.

411
00:32:35,529 --> 00:32:39,915
"You still have me... Just relax, Ms. Ya.

412
00:32:41,998 --> 00:32:43,872
"Hold here... it's safer.

413
00:32:45,206 --> 00:32:46,039
Right here!
